## Security Best Practices

- **Input validation**: Use `class-validator` + `class-transformer` in NestJS DTOs
- **Authentication**: Use `@yomcl/jwt-verify` guards (`AdminGuard`, `ReadGuard`, `StoreGuard`) — never roll custom JWT logic
- **Environment variables**: Access only via `ConfigService`, never `process.env` directly in domain or application code
- **Secrets**: Never commit `.env` files; always maintain `.env.example` with all required keys (including `TOKEN_PACKAGE`)
- **Injection prevention**: Mongoose typed schemas prevent NoSQL injection; Prisma uses parameterized queries
- **Rate limiting**: `@nestjs/throttler` for public endpoints
- **CORS**: Configure explicitly per environment; never use `*` in production
- **Multi-tenancy**: Every query must be scoped to `customerId` — treat unscoped queries as security vulnerabilities

```typescript
// NestJS DTO with validation
export class CreateBannerDto {
  @IsString()
  @IsNotEmpty()
  @MaxLength(200)
  title: string;

  @IsString()
  @IsNotEmpty()
  @MaxLength(2000)
  description: string;

  @IsOptional()
  @IsUrl()
  imageUrl?: string;
}
```

