## Development Workflow

### Git Workflow
- Main branch: `production` (protected, no direct pushes)
- Feature branches: `feature/[ticket-id]-backend`
- Bugfix branches: `fix/[ticket-id]-description`
- Commit messages follow **Conventional Commits**: `feat:`, `fix:`, `docs:`, `test:`, `refactor:`

### CI/CD
- GitHub Actions handles CI/CD
- Plan runs on PR open/update
- Apply (deploy) runs on merge to `production`

### Pre-commit Checklist
1. `npm run lint` — zero linting errors
2. `tsc --noEmit` — zero TypeScript errors
3. `npm test` — all tests pass, coverage >= 90% (NestJS services)
4. Verify `TOKEN_PACKAGE` is documented in `.env.example` if a new `@yomcl/*` package was added
5. Update `ai-specs/specs/api-spec.yml` if endpoints changed
6. Update `ai-specs/specs/data-model.md` if schema changed
7. Observability coverage — the new/changed flow emits its canonical `@yomcl/observability` event, and any stale log you touched now tells the truth (see [Observability Coverage](#observability-coverage))

### Development Scripts
```bash
npm run start:dev     # Development server with hot reload
npm run test          # Run all unit tests
npm run test:watch    # Watch mode
npm run test:cov      # With coverage report
npm run test:e2e      # End-to-end tests
npm run lint          # ESLint
npm run build         # Production build
```
